432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 154 0 R
/T (As we began testing the BaseBot after the initial assembly, a few electrical improvements became necessary to make the robot more stable and easier to maintain. These were not major redesigns, but practical refinements led by our electronics lead, Mohammed Zaid, to ensure the wiring remained clean, safe, and consistent during repeated testing. The first adjustments focused on reorganizing cable routes so that none of the wires came close to the wheels, arm joints, or the rotating gripper area. This reduced strain on connectors and prevented loose wires from interfering with movement.)
/E (As we began testing the BaseBot after the initial assembly, a few electrical improvements became necessary to make the robot more stable and easier to maintain. These were not major redesigns, but practical refinements led by our electronics lead, Mohammed Zaid, to ensure the wiring remained clean, safe, and consistent during repeated testing. The first adjustments focused on reorganizing cable routes so that none of the wires came close to the wheels, arm joints, or the rotating gripper area. This reduced strain on connectors and prevented loose wires from interfering with movement.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
