502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 161 0 R
/T (Every evening session became a pattern: upload a version of the code, power on the robot, test the motion on the floor, identify the issue, and head back to the laptop for another correction. Sometimes the robot accelerated too quickly, so the team reduced the response curve of the joysticks. Sometimes the turning radius felt too wide, so the team adjusted the turning factor inside the program. When the gripper required faster reaction time, the servo positions were fine-tuned for cleaner opening and closing. Through this continuous process, EdgeBot gradually became stable, precise, and driver-friendly.)
/E (Every evening session became a pattern: upload a version of the code, power on the robot, test the motion on the floor, identify the issue, and head back to the laptop for another correction. Sometimes the robot accelerated too quickly, so the team reduced the response curve of the joysticks. Sometimes the turning radius felt too wide, so the team adjusted the turning factor inside the program. When the gripper required faster reaction time, the servo positions were fine-tuned for cleaner opening and closing. Through this continuous process, EdgeBot gradually became stable, precise, and driver-friendly.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
