/T (The IR array became the cornerstone of our autonomous navigation. Positioned at the front, it detected light and dark surfaces, enabling the robot to recognize when it was on or off the line. This required meticulous calibration and tailored correction logic to ensure smooth adjustments without jolting or overshooting turns.)
